  "markdown": "Material family\n\n# Paper and non-woven\n\nPrinted or plain, from a quiet texture to a large repeat.\n\n![Close view of Adam's Eden wallcovering by Adam Calkin for Lewis & Wood at Brown's Hotel, Mayfair: a yellow bird on a branch above the printed selvedge.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/browns-hotel-mayfair-06.jpg)\n\nPrinted Adam’s Eden by Adam Calkin for Lewis & Wood at Brown’s Hotel, Mayfair, with its printed selvedge still visible. The repeat and edge are product-specific.Mr Wallcover project photograph.[Brown’s Hotel: the project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/browns-hotel-mayfair/)\n\nBefore you choose\n\n**Consider it when**\n: You want a printed pattern or a quieter, more even visual finish.\n\n**The trade-off**\n: Print, backing and care vary substantially between products.\n\n**Before ordering**\n: Confirm the repeat, match, usable width and actual cleaning instructions.\n\n01 · The finish\n\n## Joins\n\nSeams are part of a hung wall. The match follows the repeat: free, straight or a half-drop. Half-drop papers and murals are set out on site; the calculator gives the order quantity, not the set-out.\n\n02 · The setting\n\n## Where it belongs\n\nHomes and hotels\n\n03 · Installation\n\n## Handling\n\nThe wall has to be sound first. Lining is used when the maker or the wall requires it.\n\n04 · Living with it\n\n## Care\n\nFollow the maker. Many papers are not washable. We do not call a family washable, fire-rated or seamless unless that product’s own data says so.\n\nDigital colour is a guide. Order a cutting or a sample before you commit to a room. We can install material you have already bought, or source a family and install it. Either way, the next step is a short note about the room.\n\nIllustrative material study · confirm the actual finish with a sample\n\nPause motion\n\nSave to shortlist\n\nSaved on this device only.\n\n[Discuss this material](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=source&service=wallcovering&topic=material%3Apaper-and-non-woven) [I already have it](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=install&service=wallcovering&topic=material%3Apaper-and-non-woven)\n\nInstallation experience\n\n## On the record\n\nPrinted papers make up most of our residential record. At the [Castle of Trematon](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/trematon-castle/), between 2019 and 2022, we hung seven House of Hackney papers through the Georgian house, with lining, papered ceilings and pattern-matched full-height drops. In [a listed Georgian house in North London](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/north-london-residence/), House of Hackney's BAMBUSA in Midnight went on every wall of a guest bedroom with sloping floors, each drop set to a laser line so the bamboo reads upright.\n\nRelief papers belong to the same family: Anaglypta on the high ceilings at [Pendley Manor Hotel](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/pendley-manor-hotel/), hung first and painted afterwards, beside Cole & Son's Petroushka velvet flock, and Lincrusta relief at Trematon, aligned to a laser line. Our guide to [papering ceilings and staircases](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/papered-ceilings-and-staircases/) covers relief overhead and on a stair. The [choosing guide](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/choosing-wallcoverings/) compares paper with the other families.\n\nPlan the detail\n\n## Useful reading\n\n- [Choosing wallcoverings](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/choosing-wallcoverings/)\n\nFrom our portfolio\n\n## Selected work\n\n- [Castle of Trematon, Cornwall](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/trematon-castle/)\n- [A Georgian house in North London](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/north-london-residence/)\n- [Pendley Manor Hotel, Tring](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/pendley-manor-hotel/)\n- [House of Hackney showroom, St Michael's Clergy House](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/house-of-hackney-st-michaels/)\n- [Brown's Hotel, Mayfair](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/browns-hotel-mayfair/)\n- [Raffles London at The OWO, Whitehall](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/raffles-london-the-owo/)\n- [Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/)\n\nMakers installed\n\n## Paper and non-woven: makers we have hung\n\nEach in our own photograph of its product on the wall. A maker named here means Mr Wallcover installed that maker's product; it is not an approval, accreditation or endorsement.\n\n- ![House of Hackney's earlier Shoreditch showroom, 2019: bold floral wallpaper behind displayed furnishings.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/hoh-shoreditch-2019-01-800.webp)\n\n### House of Hackney\n\nInstalled at [About](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/) · [House of Hackney showroom, St Michael's Clergy House](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/house-of-hackney-st-michaels/) · [Private residence, Little Venice](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/private-residence-little-venice/) · [Castle of Trematon, Cornwall](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/trematon-castle/).\n\n- ![Close-up of Cole & Son Petroushka velvet flock in gold on cream, Pendley Manor Hotel, Tring.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/pendley-manor-04-800.webp)\n\n### Cole & Son\n\nInstalled at [Pendley Manor Hotel, Tring](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/pendley-manor-hotel/).\n\n- ![Freshly papered Anaglypta ceiling in a Pendley Manor room.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/pendley-manor-03-800.webp)\n\n### Anaglypta\n\nInstalled at [Pendley Manor Hotel, Tring](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/pendley-manor-hotel/).\n\n- ![Curved staircase wall during Lincrusta installation, Trematon Castle.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/trematon-ig-28-800.webp)\n\n### Lincrusta\n\nInstalled at [Castle of Trematon, Cornwall](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/trematon-castle/).\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder · Last reviewed 9 October 2026\n",
